        "original_id": "d0a73eca-d10b-5edc-a524-515b8a00e688",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Eugene Onegin, The Devil and Kate\n- People: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, Antonín Dvořák, Konstantin Shilovsky, Modest Tchaikovsky, Adolf Čech\n- Roles: composers, librettists, conductors, friends\n\nFacts:\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky composed Eugene Onegin.\n- Antonín Dvořák composed The Devil and Kate.\n- Eugene Onegin had contributions from Tchaikovsky's friends, including Konstantin Shilovsky on the libretto and Modest Tchaikovsky in shaping the work.\n- The Devil and Kate is not chiefly characterized by comparable contributions from friends of Antonín Dvořák in its making.\n- Therefore, Eugene Onegin had more contributions to its making from friends of the composer than The Devil and Kate.",
