        "original_id": "8318f490-8a46-5989-9e20-39f00c649f30",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Eugene Onegin, The Devil and Kate\n- People: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, Konstantin Shilovsky, Antonín Dvořák, Adolf Wenig\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, acts and scenes\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene Onegin is an opera by Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky.\n- Konstantin Shilovsky, a friend of Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, contributed M. Triquet's verses for Act 2, Scene 1 of Eugene Onegin.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky arranged the text for Lensky's arioso in Act 1, Scene 1 of Eugene Onegin.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky arranged almost all of Prince Gremin's aria in Act 3, Scene 1 of Eugene Onegin.\n- The Devil and Kate is an opera in three acts by Antonín Dvořák.\n- The Devil and Kate has the Czech title Čert a Káča.\n- The Devil and Kate uses a Czech libretto by Adolf Wenig.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
